      "message": "We have more problems on ARM + MSVC.\n\n`C:\\b\\s\\w\\ir\\skia\\third_party\\externals\\zlib\\crc32_simd.c(402): fatal error C1189: #error:  ARM CRC32 SIMD extensions only supported for Clang and GCC`\n\nI think this TODO might be out of date, but the if check is correct as-is.\n\nWhat we _want_ is `is_clang || is_gcc`, but surprisingly we don\u0027t have an `is_gcc` flag. We can approximate what we want by saying `is_clang || !is_win`, since we don\u0027t use GCC on Windows and don\u0027t use MSVC on anything _but_ Windows. The check we have today matches that, just stated with an extra negation for some weird reason.\n\n@thakis@chromium.org",
